Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:04:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add ms_tlsmldsacert GODEBUG setting

Default to 1 to preserve ML-DSA certificate signature advertisements.
When set to 0, omit ML-DSA-44, ML-DSA-65, and ML-DSA-87 from
signature_algorithms_cert in ClientHello and CertificateRequest,
independently of ms_tlsprofile and the crypto backend. Leave the
extension, handshake signatures, and certificate verification unchanged.

This opt-out addresses compatibility with TLS-inspecting middleboxes
that reject ML-DSA certificate signature schemes (golang/go#81199).

Test the default and both setting values on the wire across TLS versions
and Microsoft profiles. Document the setting's introduction in v1.27.2-2.
