@@ -211,6 +211,14 @@ enforcement of Extended Master Secret in FIPS 140-3 mode. There is no change in
 default behavior. This setting was backported to Go 1.26.6 and Go 1.25.13.
 We plan to remove this setting in Go 1.31.
 
+Microsoft build of Go `v1.27.2-2` added a new `ms_tlsmldsacert` setting that
+controls whether `crypto/tls` advertises ML-DSA in the `signature_algorithms_cert`
+extension. The default value is `ms_tlsmldsacert=1`. Setting
+`ms_tlsmldsacert=0` omits ML-DSA-44, ML-DSA-65, and ML-DSA-87 from this extension
+in ClientHello and CertificateRequest messages, independently of `ms_tlsprofile`.
+The extension and its other algorithms remain present. ML-DSA handshake
+signatures, ML-KEM key exchange, and certificate verification are unaffected.
+
 ### Go 1.26
 
 Go 1.26 added a new `httpcookiemaxnum` setting that controls the maximum number
